  "api_writes": "3 — each one repository_dispatch through the fleet-write relay (POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/dispatches), executed as objectstack-fleet[bot]: (1) pr_create, POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/pulls (draft, PR #20243); (2) label-write --assign os-sales, POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/issues/20243/assignees; (3) this os-dev-report comment, POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/issues/20212/comments. Plus git push (not REST). Reads were plain REST GETs.",
  "open_questions": [
    {
      "question": "Triage execution note 1 asks to pin the five predicates on SqlDriver AND InMemoryDriver. A plugin-security test importing @objectstack/driver-memory is an unledgered driver-memory consumer, and check:driver-memory-census says consumer legitimacy is a maintainer ruling. How should the InMemoryDriver cell land?",
      "options": [
        "A: the maintainer rules plugin-security's RLS pin a driver-memory test consumer; the census gains the entry and ruling marker, and the cell returns (one DRIVERS row + devDependency + vitest alias; the code was written and ran green, 102 cases)",
        "B: put the InMemoryDriver cell in driver-memory's own test side, with devDependencies on @objectstack/objectql and @objectstack/plugin-security (census-clean, no cycle measured, but the lowest-level driver would dev-depend on a plugin and pull its closure into its CI shard)",
        "C: keep the SqlDriver-only pin as landed. The refusal happens in the compile step before any driver is asked, the compileFilter unit pin holds that step, and the InMemoryDriver and PostgreSQL readings are recorded on the PR"
      ],
      "recommendation": "C. Business need: the defect is driver-independent by construction now, and no stored policy in this repo carries these shapes. Long-term: it keeps the driver-memory retirement bookkeeping intact rather than adding a consumer to a ledger built to shrink. AI-error resistance: the unit pin fails for any driver the moment the compile step stops refusing. Scope: A adds a maintainer ruling and B an inverted dev-dependency, each for a cell measured once. If the maintainer wants the matrix, A is a mechanical follow-up."
    },
    {
      "question": "The two pending changesets 19951-rls-lint-per-request-refusals.md and 20018-native-read-scope-faces.md each got a one-clause DELIBERATE CORRECTION because this change made a sentence in them false. check-empty-changeset stays red on both by design. Confirm the corrections?",
      "options": [
        "A: confirm as written (both now describe the drop / deny-sentinel answer)",
        "B: reword",
        "C: restore (would republish a false sentence)"
      ],
      "recommendation": "A, because the corrected sentences are measured at head (read 0 rows + WARN, check 403, analytics 0 rows on all three faces) and restoring would put a false statement into the release notes."
    }
  ],
